# OneOhm — Engineering Law

> **Search first. Pattern match. Never duplicate. Test everything.**

---

## 🔴 Before ANY Change

1. **Search** — `grep` existing code. If it exists, use it.
2. **Read** — Understand context. Read related files.
3. **Match** — Follow existing patterns exactly.
4. **Extract** — Used 2+ times? Move to `shared/` or `common/`.
5. **Ask** — Uncertain? Clarify. Never guess.

---

## 🏗️ Monorepo Structure

```
apps/backend/     → NestJS + TypeORM + PostgreSQL
apps/web/         → Next.js 15 + TanStack Query + Zustand
libs/shared-types/   → Enums, interfaces (BOTH apps use)
libs/shared-utils/   → Backend helpers
libs/shared-ui/      → Reusable React components
```

**Types Location:**
| Scope | Path |
|-------|------|
| Shared | `@oneohm-epc/shared-types` |
| Backend only | `modules/[feature]/types/` |
| Frontend only | `lib/types/` |

---

## 📛 Naming

| Item | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Files | kebab-case | `customer-profile.entity.ts` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `CustomerProfileEntity` |
| Functions | camelCase | `findByOrganization` |
| DB columns | snake_case | `organization_id` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE | `ACCESS_TOKEN_KEY` |

---

## 🚫 NEVER

```
❌ any type         → Use proper types
❌ Duplicate code   → Search & reuse
❌ TypeORM in service → Use repository
❌ console.log      → Use Logger
❌ Hardcoded values → Use enums/env
❌ No pagination    → Always paginate lists
❌ No soft delete   → deletedAt IS NULL
❌ No audit         → createdBy/updatedBy
❌ Business logic in controller/component
```

---

## ✅ Quality Gate

Every change MUST:
- Match codebase patterns
- Handle errors gracefully
- Be typed (no `any`)
- Pass lint
- Be tested (see below)

